Based on my review of your Quick Bill app's current architecture, you have a very solid foundation! You’ve already built a robust offline-first Point of Sale (POS) application using Hive for local storage, flutter_bloc for state management, mobile_scanner for barcodes, and print_bluetooth_thermal for receipts.

To transition this from a capable project into a highly competitive, market-ready product (like Khatabook, Vyapar, or Square), here is a strategic roadmap of features you should implement:

1. Essential Core Features (To hit the market quickly)
These features are expected by almost all retail shop owners:

Inventory Management & Low Stock Alerts: Your Product entity has a stock field, but you need to build out an active inventory management screen. Add push notifications or a dashboard alert when items drop below a predefined threshold.
Taxation & GST Support: Add customizable tax rates (e.g., GST, VAT) at the product level and aggregate them on the final bill. Make it configurable in the Shop settings so users in different regions can adapt it.
Daily Analytics & Reports: A dashboard showing "Today's Sales", "Top Selling Items", and "Total Profit" is a major selling point. Retailers want to see their business growth at a glance.
2. Digital Upgrades (To stand out from legacy systems)
Digital Receipts (WhatsApp Integration): While you have thermal printing, adding a button to "Share Invoice via WhatsApp" (as a PDF or text message) is a massive cost-saver for shop owners who don't want to buy paper rolls. You can implement this using the url_launcher package.
Dynamic UPI QR Code Generation: You already have the upiId in the Shop model. You can use the pretty_qr_code package (which is already in your pubspec.yaml) to generate a dynamic UPI QR code on the billing screen. The QR code should embed the total bill amount so the customer just scans and pays without entering the amount manually.
3. Monetization & Cloud Strategy (To build a SaaS business)
Currently, your app is 100% offline (using Hive). This is a great feature, but limits you to a single device.

Cloud Backup & Sync (Premium Tier): Integrate Firebase (Firestore) or Supabase. Allow shop owners to back up their data to the cloud. You can offer the offline version for free, and charge a monthly subscription for Cloud Sync across multiple devices.
Bulk Import/Export (CSV/Excel): Allow users to import their existing product lists from an Excel/CSV file instead of adding hundreds of items manually. Provide an export feature so they can send sales data to their accountant (e.g., for Tally integration).
4. Advanced "Khata" (Credit) System
Customer Management & Ledgers: In many markets (especially India and Southeast Asia), customers buy on credit ("Udhar"). Creating a Customer entity and tracking their pending balances (Khata) will make your app essential to their daily operations.
